<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aravidu dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1570–<a href="/years/1646">1646</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Aravidu dynasty was the fourth and last ruling house of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vijayanagara-empire">Vijayanagara Empire</a>. Founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tirumala-deva-raya">Tirumala Deva Raya</a>, brother of the regent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aliya-rama-raya">Aliya Rama Raya</a> who fell at Talikota in 1565, it ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/penukonda">Penukonda</a> and later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chandragiri">Chandragiri</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vellore">Vellore</a> while the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nayaka">Nayaka</a> governors of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madurai">Madurai</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thanjavur">Thanjavur</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gingee">Gingee</a> became independent. Its last king, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sriranga-iii">Sriranga III</a>, lost his lands by 1646.</p></div>
